(This report documents the current architecture and implementation status of the fusion layer) Tj
0 -14 Td
(for the Cyber Analytics multi-model email threat system. The fusion layer is the terminal) Tj
0 -14 Td
(decision component that combines model probabilities from the header, body, and malware) Tj
0 -14 Td
(branches into one final threat score and classification output. The implementation is) Tj
0 -14 Td
(intentionally late-fusion and production-oriented for Phase 1, emphasizing modularity,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(explainability, robust handling of partial modality availability, and operational) Tj
0 -14 Td
(compatibility with cloud event-driven workflows.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(The fusion layer currently supports two fusion strategies: logistic regression stacking) Tj
0 -14 Td
(\(primary\) and soft voting \(baseline\). It enforces strict input and output contracts,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(validates data quality, handles missing malware probabilities for emails without) Tj
0 -14 Td
(attachments, maps final scores to project-defined risk levels, and returns an explainable) Tj
0 -14 Td
(output record that includes both the fusion method and the set of modalities used.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
